# Vauxhall Viva five-door hatchback, 2015-2019.
#
# The revived Viva: the budget city car built by Opel in Eisenach and sold in
# Britain from June 2015 to 2019, when the Corsa took the entry position.
# Not to be confused with the 1963-79 Viva of the same name.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Viva
#
# Dimensions 3.675 x 1.698 x 1.476 m, wheelbase 2.385 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a TRUE level side elevation, within 3 degrees.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was read. White, Red, Blue and
# Silver are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
#
# Speed 170 km/h. Comfort 60/420, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 60. Classes 0,1.
# Dates: intro June 2015; retires staggered 2027-2030 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-viva-2015.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-viva-2015.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-viva-2015/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the standard five-door hatchback is modelled. The
# pressed body contours, the lamp internals and the wheel trim are simplified.
# One representative wheel design stands for all trims.


